{"step_index":77,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-28T17:04:22Z","thinking":"**Constructing Full Project Script**\n\nI've got a solid plan: I'm writing `build_project.py` now. It'll handle everything – backend, frontend, database, the works. Using `write_to_file` and then running it is clean and robust, and gives us perfect control over formatting.\n\n\n**Designing Database Structure**\n\nI'm deep in the database schema now, fleshing out `backend/database.py`. It's going to use SQLite with WAL mode, and I'm designing the tables. I'm building out auto-creation for tables including `trips`, `destinations`, `natpac_surveys`, and `tourism_cache`. For the `destinations` table, I'm seeding rich data for Kerala and Southern India destinations. The goal is a robust and complete data structure.\n\n\n**Defining AI Interactions**\n\nI'm now outlining `backend/models.py` and `backend/ai_service.py`. The models include `TripCreate`, `AIRouteResponse`, and more, using Pydantic for validation and serialization. I've integrated OpenAI and Gemini support with API keys, along with regex/NLP-based stop extraction for route generation and Google Routes API fallback. I'm focusing on robust request/response structures for AI-driven functionality.\n\n\n**Integrating Tourism Features**\n\nI'm now integrating robust tourism features, focusing on `backend/tourism_service.py`. I've added functions to call public APIs. I'm using OpenStreetMap, Wikivoyage and Wikipedia for detailed geocoding, and weather data for real-world tourism information. This will support itinerary generation. I'm building out a natural language trip parser to translate user input to trip parameters like origin, destination, and travel mode. I'm also planning an AI-powered itinerary generator.\n\n\n**Implementing API Endpoints**\n\nI'm now implementing the full API with FastAPI in `backend/app.py`. CORS is enabled. I've built the expanded endpoints: the AI route, the trip-related operations, the setup and status routes, plus the new natural language trip parsing and itinerary generation. Also, I've extended tourism-related endpoints and added the analytics endpoints with CSV export, alongside geocoding routes. It's a comprehensive and fully-featured API. I'm focusing on serving the static frontend now.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Comprehensive project build script that constructs the entire Python FastAPI backend, database, services, models, and dependencies.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import os\nimport json\nimport base64\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nWORKSPACE = Path(r\"C:\\Users\\akhil\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\")\nBACKEND = WORKSPACE / \"backend\"\nFRONTEND = WORKSPACE / \"frontend\"\nSRC = FRONTEND / \"src\"\nCOMPONENTS = SRC / \"components\"\nDATA = WORKSPACE / \"data\"\n\nfor d in [BACKEND, FRONTEND, SRC, COMPONENTS, DATA]:\n    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. backend/__init__.py\n# -------------------------------------------------------------\n(BACKEND / \"__init__.py\").write_text('\"\"\"TripTrail NATPAC Backend Package\"\"\"\\n', encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2. backend/database.py\n# -------------------------------------------------------------\ndb_code = '''import os\nimport json\nimport sqlite3\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nDB_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / 'data'\nDB_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nSQLITE_PATH = DB_DIR / 'triptrail.db'\nDATABASE_URL = os.getenv('DATABASE_URL')\n\ndef get_connection():\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(str(SQLITE_PATH), timeout=15.0, check_same_thread=False)\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    conn.execute('PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;')\n    conn.execute('PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;')\n    return conn\n\ndef init_db():\n    with get_connection() as conn:\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        \n        # 1. Trips table (supports original schema + NATPAC fields)\n        cursor.execute(\\'\\'\\'\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS trips (\n                id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                title TEXT NOT NULL,\n                location TEXT NOT NULL,\n                start_date TEXT NOT NULL,\n                end_date TEXT NOT NULL,\n                note TEXT DEFAULT '',\n                mood TEXT DEFAULT 'sunny',\n                created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now', 'localtime')),\n                trip_number INTEGER DEFAULT 1,\n                origin TEXT DEFAULT '',\n                destination TEXT DEFAULT '',\n                departure_time TEXT DEFAULT '',\n                arrival_time TEXT DEFAULT '',\n                travel_mode TEXT DEFAULT 'Bus',\n                trip_purpose TEXT DEFAULT 'Tourism',\n                passenger_count INTEGER DEFAULT 1,\n                fare_cost REAL DEFAULT 0.0,\n                distance_km REAL DEFAULT 0.0,\n                duration_min INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n                origin_lat REAL,\n                origin_lng REAL,\n                dest_lat REAL,\n                dest_lng REAL,\n                is_auto_detected INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n                is_synced INTEGER DEFAULT 1,\n                gps_trace_json TEXT DEFAULT '[]'\n            );\n        \\'\\'\\')\n        \n        # 2. Destinations & Tourism Records table\n        cursor.execute(\\'\\'\\'\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS destinations (\n                id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                name TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n                state_region TEXT DEFAULT 'Kerala',\n                category TEXT DEFAULT 'Tourism',\n                description TEXT DEFAULT '',\n                latitude REAL DEFAULT 0.0,\n                longitude REAL DEFAULT 0.0,\n                food_cuisine TEXT DEFAULT '[]',\n                attractions TEXT DEFAULT '[]',\n                hotels TEXT DEFAULT '[]',\n                activities TEXT DEFAULT '[]',\n                ratings REAL DEFAULT 4.5,\n                approx_cost_per_day REAL DEFAULT 2000.0,\n                best_season TEXT DEFAULT 'Oct - Mar',\n                weather_summary TEXT DEFAULT 'Pleasant',\n                image_url TEXT DEFAULT '',\n                source TEXT DEFAULT 'local_cache',\n                updated_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now', 'localtime'))\n            );\n        \\'\\'\\')\n        \n        # 3. NATPAC Transportation Surveys table\n        cursor.execute(\\'\\'\\'\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS natpac_surveys (\n                id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                user_id TEXT DEFAULT 'anonymous',\n                age_group TEXT DEFAULT '18-35',\n                gender TEXT DEFAULT 'Unspecified',\n                occupation TEXT DEFAULT 'Working Professional',\n                monthly_travel_budget REAL DEFAULT 3000.0,\n                frequent_mode TEXT DEFAULT 'Bus / Public Transport',\n                feedback TEXT DEFAULT '',\n                created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now', 'localtime'))\n            );\n        \\'\\'\\')\n\n        # 4. API Tourism Cache table\n        cursor.execute(\\'\\'\\'\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tourism_cache (\n                cache_key TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n                data_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n                cached_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now', 'localtime')),\n                expires_at TEXT\n            );\n        \\'\\'\\')\n        \n        cursor.execute('CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_trips_start_date ON trips(start_date DESC);')\n        cursor.execute('CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_trips_mode ON trips(travel_mode);')\n        cursor.execute('CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_destinations_name ON destinations(name);')\n        cursor.execute('CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_destinations_region ON destinations(state_region);')\n        \n        conn.commit()\n        seed_destinations_if_empty(cursor, conn)\n        seed_sample_trips_if_empty(cursor, conn)\n\ndef seed_destinations_if_empty(cursor, conn):\n    cursor.execute('SELECT COUNT(*) as cnt FROM destinations;')\n    if cursor.fetchone()['cnt'] > 0:\n        return\n\n    sample_destinations = [\n        {\n            'name': 'Munnar',\n            'state_region': 'Kerala (Idukki)',\n            'category': 'Hill Station & Tea Plantations',\n            'description': 'Munnar is a picturesque hill station in the Western Ghats known for lush tea estates, misty valleys, waterfalls, and rare flora like Neelakurinji.',\n            'latitude': 10.0889,\n            'longitude': 77.0595,\n            'food_cuisine': json.dumps([\n                'Kerala Parotta with Veg/Chicken Curry',\n                'Puttu and Kadala Curry',\n                'Fresh Cardamom & Ginger Tea',\n                'Spiced Hot Banana Fritters (Pazham Pori)',\n                'Local Roasted Cashews & Homemade Chocolates'\n            ]),\n            'attractions': json.dumps([\n                'Eravikulam National Park (Nilgiri Tahr sanctuary)',\n                'Mattupetty Dam & Eco Point',\n                'Tea Museum & Tata Tea Estate',\n                'Top Station Panorama Viewpoint',\n                'Attukad & Lakkam Waterfalls'\n            ]),\n            'hotels': json.dumps([\n                {'name': 'Tea County Munnar (KTDC)', 'type': 'Heritage / Mid-Range', 'price_range': '₹4,500 - ₹7,000/night', 'rating': 4.6},\n                {'name': 'Blanket Hotel & Spa', 'type': 'Luxury Resort', 'price_range': '₹9,000 - ₹15,000/night', 'rating': 4.8},\n                {'name': 'Munnar Green Homestay', 'type': 'Budget Homestay', 'price_range': '₹1,500 - ₹2,500/night', 'rating': 4.4}\n            ]),\n            'activities': json.dumps([\n                'Tea Plantation Trekking & Est